a shot to the heart by a man with a  homemade gun  a routine campaign speech ending in an  unprecedented assassination  former japanese prime minister shinzo  abe died friday morning in the western  city of nara he was campaigning for  upper house elections scheduled for  sunday  seconds after abe collapsed officers  tackled the suspect  police say 41 year old tatsuya yamagami  told them he was disgruntled with abe  and aimed to kill him  it was a rare occurrence in a country  with a low crime rate and some of the  world's most restrictive gun laws  we cannot accept that this violent act  took place during an election  the foundation of democracy  in the strongest terms i condemn this  attack  the 67 year old was a dynamo of japanese  politics and a third generation  politician  his grandfather was prime minister his  father foreign minister  abe distinguished himself as the  longest-serving prime minister with two  terms in office  he brought stability to a political  system that tended to kind of churn out  prime ministers one after another  not only that but he was also  transformative in japanese politics he  made japan a much more significant  player in terms of regional and i would  say even global security  abe promoted policies dubbed ubenomics  intended to boost the economy  he wanted to strengthen japan's  geopolitical clout by amending its  post-world war ii pacifist constitution  it proved polarizing among the public  and his efforts failed  during his last year in office he was  criticized for his handling of the kovit  19 pandemic  worked hard every single day to  revitalize the economy and to conduct  diplomacy that would protect the  national interest  during this time i'm proud to have taken  on various challenges with the japanese  people  although he resigned in 2020 citing poor  health the following year abe returned  as leader of the liberal democratic  party a man who couldn't shed his  political skin  assassinated for it natasha name al  jazeera
 

